From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opi5 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rga: add KUnit tests

rga_kunit (ROCKCHIP_RGA_KUNIT_TEST), with literal values rather than the
driver's macros:

- rga_request: rga_request_check refuses id 0, no tasks or no task
  pointer with -EINVAL and more than 256 tasks with -EFBIG.
- rga_mm_sgt: a one-segment sg_table is accepted, two non-mergeable
  segments are -EOPNOTSUPP (2010's single-base rule).

rga3.ko fails to load without RGA cores (rga_iommu_bind returns -EFAULT),
so a test module that needs it can't run in QEMU. Both checks become
static inlines in the headers instead, rga_request_check moved from
rga_job.c and the nents check of rga_mm_map_virt_addr as
rga_mm_check_sgt_single_base, and rga_kunit includes them. The driver
compiles the same code.
